 is \\( 6 \\times 7 = 42 \\) inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given perimeter of one equilateral triangle\nperimeter_triangle = 21\n\n# Calculate side length of the equilateral triangle\nside_length_triangle = perimeter_triangle / 3\n\n# Since the side length of the hexagon is the same as the side length of the equilateral triangle\nside_length_hexagon = side_length_triangle\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = 6 * side_length_hexagon\nprint(perimeter_hexagon)\n```\n```output\n42.0\n```\nThe perimeter of the regular hexagon is \\(\\boxed{42}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the side length of the equilateral triangle.\n2. Use the side length to find the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n\nSince the perimeter of one equilateral triangle is 21 inches, and an equilateral triangle has three equal sides, the side length of the triangle is \\( \\frac{21}{3} = 7 \\) inches. \n\nA regular hexagon is made up of six such equilateral triangles, so the side length of the hexagon is the same as the side length of the triangle, which is 7 inches. The perimeter of the hexagon is then \\( 6 \\times 7 = 42 \\) inches.\n\nLet's write the Python code to confirm this calculation.\n\n```python\n# Calculate the side length of the equilateral triangle\nperimeter_triangle = 21\nside_length_triangle = perimeter_triangle / 3\n\n# The side length of the hexagon is the same as the side length of the triangle\nside_length_hexagon = side_length_triangle\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = 6 * side_length_hexagon\n\n# Output the result\nprint(perimeter_hexagon)\n```\n```output\n42.0\n```\nThe perimeter of the regular hexagon is \\(\\boxed{42}\\) inches.", 'A regular hexagon can be divided into six equilateral triangles. If the perimeter of one of the triangles is 21 inches, then each side of the equilateral triangle is 21/3 = 7 inches. Since 