 \\]\n\nSo, the side length of the octagon is 12 cm. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the perimeter of the regular hexagon.\n2. Use the perimeter of the hexagon to determine the side length of the regular octagon.\n\nA regular hexagon has six equal sides. Given that each side of the hexagon is 16 cm, the perimeter of the hexagon is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm.\n\nA regular octagon has eight equal sides. Since the perimeter of the octagon is the same as the perimeter of the hexagon, the perimeter of the octagon is also 96 cm. Therefore, the length of each side of the octagon is \\( \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\) cm.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = 6 * side_length_hexagon\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / 8\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe length of each side of the octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve this problem, we need to find the side length of a regular octagon that has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm.\n\n1. First, we calculate the perimeter of the hexagon. Since a hexagon has 6 sides, and each side is 16 cm, the perimeter of the hexagon is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm.\n2. Next, we know that the octagon has 8 sides and the 