\n   - Since the perimeters of the hexagon and the octagon are equal:\n     \\[\n     6 \\times 16 = 8 \\times s\n     \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\( s \\):**\n   - Rearrange the equation to solve for \\( s \\):\n     \\[\n     s = \\frac{6 \\times 16}{8}\n     \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python and SymPy to ensure accuracy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the side length of the hexagon\nside_hexagon = 16\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = 6 * side_hexagon\n\n# Define the number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\n\n# Print the side length of the octagon\nprint(side_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the regular octagon that has the same perimeter as the regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm is \\(\\boxed{12 \\text{ cm}}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to determine the side length of a regular octagon that has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm.\n\n1. First, we calculate the perimeter of the hexagon. Since a hexagon has 6 sides, the perimeter \\(P_{\\text{hexagon}}\\) is:\n   \\[\n   P_{\\text{hexagon}} = 6 \\times 16 \\text{ cm} = 96 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. The perimeter of the octagon is the same as the perimeter of the hexagon, so the perimeter \\(P_{\\text{octagon}}\\) of the octagon is also 96 cm. Since an octagon has 8 sides, the side length \\(s\\) of the octagon can be calculated as:\n   \\[\n   P_{\\text{octagon}} = 8 \\times s = 96 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(s\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   s = \\frac{96 \\text{ cm}}{8} = 12 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\nSo, the side length of the octagon is \\(12\\) cm. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = 6 * side_length_hexagon\n\n# The perimeter of the octagon is the