p process:\n\n1. Set up the division problem:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n   & x^5 & -x^4 & +x^3 & -x^2 & +x & -1 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   x+1 & x^6 & & & & & -3 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n2. Divide the leading term of the dividend by the leading term of the divisor to get the first term of the quotient:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x^6}{x} = x^5\n   \\]\n3. Multiply the entire divisor by this term and subtract the result from the dividend:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n   & x^5 & -x^4 & +x^3 & -x^2 & +x & -1 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   x+1 & x^6 & & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & x^6 & +x^5 & & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & -x^5 & & & & -3 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n4. Repeat the process with the new polynomial:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{-x^5}{x} = -x^4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n   & x^5 & -x^4 & +x^3 & -x^2 & +x & -1 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   x+1 & x^6 & & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & x^6 & +x^5 & & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & -x^5 & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & & -x^5 & -x^4 & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & & x^4 & & & -3 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n5. Continue this process until the degree of the remainder is less than the degree of the divisor:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{x^4}{x} = x^3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n   & x^5 & -x^4 & +x^3 & -x^2 & +x & -1 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   x+1 & x^6 & & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & x^6 & +x^5 & & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & -x^5 & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & & -x^5 & -x^4 & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & & x^4 & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & & & x^4 & +x^3 & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & & & -x^3 & & -3 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{-x^3}{x} = -x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n   & x^5 & -x^4 & +x^3 & -x^2 & +x & -1 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   x+1 & x^6 & & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & x^6 & +x^5 & & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & -x^5 & & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & & -x^5 & -x^4 & & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & & x^4 & & & -3 \\\\\n   - & & & x^4 & +x^3 & & \\\\\n   \\hline\n   & & & & -x^3 & & -3 \\\\\n   - & & & & -x^3 & -x^2 & \\\\\n 