ting the terms where the exponent of \\(e^{i(7-2k)x}\\) is an integer multiple of \\(2\\pi i\\), which corresponds to the sine terms. Specifically, we are interested in the coefficients of \\(e^{7ix}\\), \\(e^{5ix}\\), \\(e^{3ix}\\), and \\(e^{ix}\\).\n\nThe terms that contribute to \\(\\sin 7x\\) are those where \\(7-2k = 7\\), which gives \\(k = 0\\). The term is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{-128i} \\binom{7}{0} (-1)^0 e^{7ix} = \\frac{1}{-128i} e^{7ix} = -\\frac{1}{128i} e^{7ix}.\n\\]\nSince \\(e^{7ix} = \\cos 7x + i \\sin 7x\\), the coefficient of \\(\\sin 7x\\) is \\(-\\frac{1}{128i} \\cdot i = \\frac{1}{128}\\).\n\nThe terms that contribute to \\(\\sin 5x\\) are those where \\(7-2k = 5\\), which gives \\(k = 1\\). The term is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{-128i} \\binom{7}{1} (-1)^1 e^{5ix} = \\frac{1}{-128i} \\cdot 7 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot e^{5ix} = \\frac{7}{128i} e^{5ix}.\n\\]\nSince \\(e^{5ix} = \\cos 5x + i \\sin 5x\\), the coefficient of \\(\\sin 5x\\) is \\(\\frac{7}{128i} \\cdot i = \\frac{7}{128}\\).\n\nThe terms that contribute to \\(\\sin 3x\\) are those where \\(7-2k = 3\\), which gives \\(k = 2\\). The term is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{-128i} \\binom{7}{2} (-1)^2 e^{3ix} = \\frac{1}{-128i} \\cdot 21 \\cdot 1 \\cdot e^{3ix} = -\\frac{21}{128i} e^{3ix}.\n\\]\nSince \\(e^{3ix} = \\cos 3x + i \\sin 3x\\), the coefficient of \\(\\sin 3x\\) is \\(-\\frac{21}{128i} \\cdot i = \\frac{21}{128}\\).\n\nThe terms that contribute to \\(\\sin x\\) are those where \\(7-2k = 1\\), which gives \\(k = 3\\). The term is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{-128i} \\binom{7}{3} (-1)^3 e^{ix} = \\frac{1}{-128i} \\cdot 35 \\cdot (-1) \\cdot e^{ix} = \\frac{35}{128i} e^{ix}.\n\\]\nSince \\(e^{ix} = \\cos x + i \\sin x\\), the coefficient of \\(\\sin x\\) is \\(\\frac{35}{128i} \\cdot i = \\frac{35}{128}\\).\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\\[\n(\\sin x)^7 = \\frac{1}{128} \\sin 7x + \\frac{7}{128} \\sin 5x + \\frac{21}{128} \\sin 3x + \\frac{35}{128} \\sin x.\n\\]\nSo, the constant \\(d\\) is \\(\\frac{35}{128}\\).\n\nLet's confirm th