inator is:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\nUsing the identity $\\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B = \\sin(A + B)$, we can rewrite the first two terms and the last two terms:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\sin(5^\\circ + 20^\\circ) = \\sin 25^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n-\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = -(\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ) = -\\sin(35^\\circ + 50^\\circ) = -\\sin 85^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSo the denominator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ\n\\]\n\n### Simplifying the Expression\nNow we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ}{\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ}\n\\]\n\nUsing the sum-to-product identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A + \\cos B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A + B}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{A - B}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A - \\sin B = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{A + B}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{A - B}{2}\\right)\n\\]\n\nWe can rewrite the numerator and the denominator:\n\\[\n\\cos 25^\\circ + \\cos 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos (-30^\\circ) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 25^\\circ - \\sin 85^\\circ = 2 \\cos \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ + 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{25^\\circ - 85^\\circ}{2}\\right) = 2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin (-30^\\circ) = -2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ}{-2 \\cos 55^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{-\\sin 30^\\circ} = -\\cot 30^\\circ = -\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nSince $\\tan \\theta = -\\sqrt{3}$, the least positive angle $\\theta$ that satisfies this equation is:\n\\[\n\\theta = 180^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ\n\\]