 "Given the function \\( F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i} \\), we need to find the value of \\( z_{2002} \\) where \\( z_n = F(z_{n-1}) \\) and \\( z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\).\n\nLet's start by calculating the first few terms of the sequence to see if there is a pattern.\n\n1. Calculate \\( z_1 = F(z_0) \\):\n\\[ z_1 = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( z_2 = F(z_1) \\):\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74825}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74826 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37413}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( z_3 = F(z_2) \\):\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\frac{37413}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37413}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37413}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37413}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} = \\frac{37413 + 37266i}{37413 - 37264i} \\]\nAgain, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{(37413 + 37266i)(37413 + 37264i)}{(37413 - 37264i)(37413 + 37264i)} = \\frac{1399756569 + 1399756528i + 1399756528i - 1388761224}{1399756569 + 1388761216} = \\frac{1100053745 + 2799513056i}{2788517785} = \\frac{1}{137} + i = z_0 \\]\n\nWe see that \\( z_3 = z_0 \\). This indicates that the sequence is periodic with a period of 3. Therefore, \\( z_{2002} = z_{2002 \\mod 3} = z_1 \\).\n\nSo, \\( z_{2002} = 1 + 274i \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the function F(z)\ndef F(z):\n    return (z + 1j) / (z - 1j)\n\n# Initial value z0\nz0 = 1/137 + 1j\n\n# Calculate z1, z2, z3 to check the periodicity\nz1 = F(z0)\nz2 = F(z1)\nz3 = F(z2)\n\n# Check the periodicity\nprint((z0, z1, z2, z3))\n```\n```output\n((0.