 + \\frac{1}{37265}i. \\]\n\n3. Compute \\( z_3 = F(z_2) \\):\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i}. \\]\nTo simplify, multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i\\right)\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)} = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37263^2 + 37266 \\cdot 37264i}{37265^2}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{37263^2 + 37264^2}{37265^2}\\right)} = \\frac{37263^2 + 37266 \\cdot 37264i}{37263^2 + 37264^2}. \\]\nSince \\( 37263^2 + 37266 \\cdot 37264i \\approx 37265^2 \\), we can see that \\( z_3 \\approx 1 + i \\).\n\n4. Compute \\( z_4 = F(z_3) \\):\n\\[ z_4 = \\frac{1 + i + i}{1 + i - i} = \\frac{1 + 2i}{1} = 1 + 2i. \\]\n\n5. Compute \\( z_5 = F(z_4) \\):\n\\[ z_5 = \\frac{1 + 2i + i}{1 + 2i - i} = \\frac{1 + 3i}{1 + i}. \\]\nTo simplify, multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_5 = \\frac{(1 + 3i)(1 - i)}{(1 + i)(1 - i)} = \\frac{1 - i + 3i + 3}{1 + 1} = \\frac{4 + 2i}{2} = 2 + i. \\]\n\n6. Compute \\( z_6 = F(z_5) \\):\n\\[ z_6 = \\frac{2 + i + i}{2 + i - i} = \\frac{2 + 2i}{2} = 1 + i. \\]\n\nWe can see that \\( z_6 = z_3 \\), and since \\( z_3 \\approx 1 + i \\), we can conclude that the sequence \\( z_n \\) is periodic with a period of 3. Therefore, \\( z_{2002} = z_{2002 \\mod 3} = z_1 \\).\n\nSo, \\( z_{2002} = 1 + 274i \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1 + 274i}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function F(z)\ndef F(z):\n    return (z + 1j) / (z - 1j)\n\n# Initial value z0\nz0 = 1/137 + 1j\n\n# Compute the first few values to check for periodicity\nz1 = F(z0)\nz2 = F(z1)