ce \\( z_1 = 1 + 274i \\), we have:\n\\[ z_{2002} = 1 + 274i. \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1 + 274i}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to analyze the function \\( F(z) = \\frac{z + i}{z - i} \\) and its iterations. We are given \\( z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i \\), and we need to find \\( z_{2002} \\).\n\nFirst, let's compute the first few iterations of \\( F(z) \\) to see if there is a pattern.\n\n1. Compute \\( z_1 = F(z_0) \\):\n\\[ z_1 = \\frac{z_0 + i}{z_0 - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 274i \\]\n\n2. Compute \\( z_2 = F(z_1) \\):\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{z_1 + i}{z_1 - i} = \\frac{1 + 274i + i}{1 + 274i - i} = \\frac{1 + 275i}{1 + 273i} \\]\nTo simplify this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_2 = \\frac{(1 + 275i)(1 - 273i)}{(1 + 273i)(1 - 273i)} = \\frac{1 - 273i + 275i + 74525}{1 + 74529} = \\frac{74526 + 2i}{74530} = \\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i \\]\n\n3. Compute \\( z_3 = F(z_2) \\):\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{z_2 + i}{z_2 - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i + i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{1}{37265}i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i}{\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i} \\]\nAgain, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ z_3 = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37266}{37265}i\\right)\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} - \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265} + \\frac{37264}{37265}i\\right)} \\]\n\\[ = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{37266}{37265}\\right)\\left(\\frac{37264}{37265}\\right)i + \\left(\\frac{37266}{37265}\\right)\\left(\\frac{37264}{37265}\\right)i - \\left(\\frac{37266}{37265}\\right)^2}{\\left(\\frac{37263}{37265}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{37264}{37265}\\right)^2} \\]\n\\[ = \\fr