p track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, give the number in the new base.\n\nLet\'s convert $555_{10}$ to base $5$:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, which gives a quotient of 111 and a remainder of 0.\n2. Divide 111 by 5, which gives a quotient of 22 and a remainder of 1.\n3. Divide 22 by 5, which gives a quotient of 4 and a remainder of 2.\n4. Divide 4 by 5, which gives a quotient of 0 and a remainder of 4.\n\nReading the remainders in reverse order, we get the base 5 representation of 555.\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python to ensure the result is accurate.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, give the number in the new base.\n\nLet\'s convert \\(555_{10}\\) to base \\(5\\):\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, which gives a quotient of 111 and a remainder of 0.\n2. Divide 111 by 5, which gives a quotient of 22 and a remainder of 1.\n3. Divide 22 by 5, which gives a quotient of 4 and a remainder of 2.\n4. Divide 4 by 5, which gives a quotient of 0 and a remainder of 4.\n\nReading the remainders in reverse order, we get \\(4210_5\\).\n\nSo, \\(555_{10}\\) in base 5 is \\(4210_5\\).\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\r\n    if n == 0:\r\n        return "0"\r\n    digits = []\r\n    while n:\r\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\r\n        n //= base\r\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\r\n\r\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\r\ndecimal_number = 555\r\nbase = 5\r\nbase_5_number = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\r\nprint(base_5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe conversion of \\(555_{10}\\) to base 5 is indeed \\(4210_5\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert the decimal number $555_{10}$ to base $5$, we need to repeatedly divide the number by $5$ and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base $5$ representation.\n\nHere is the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, which gives a quotient of 111 and a remainder of 0.\n2. Divide 111 by 5, which gives a quotient of 22 and a remainder of 1.\n3. Divide 22 by 5, which gives a quotient of 4 and a remainder of 2.\n4. Divide 4 by 5, which gives a quotient of 0 and a remainder of 4.\n\nReading the remainders in reverse order, we get the base $5$ representation of $555_{10}$ as $4210_5$.\n\nLet\'s verify this using Python code.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 5))\n        n //= 5\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from decimal to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase5_number = decimal_to_base5(decimal_number)\nprint(base5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base $5$ representation of the decimal number $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the base and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, give the number in the new base. Let\'s convert \\(555_{10}\\) to base 5 using this method.\n\nHere\'s the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, which gives a quotient of 111 and a remainder of 0.\n2. Divide 111 by 5, which gives a quotient of 22 and a remainder of 1.\n3. Divide 22 by 5, which gives a quotient of 4 and a remainder of 2.\n4. Divide 4 by 5, which gives a quotient of 0 and a remainder of 4.\n\nThe remainders, read in reverse order, give the base 5 representation of 555. So, \\(555_{10} = 4210_5\\).\n\nLet\'s verify this by implementing the conversion in Python.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process for $555_{10}$ to base $5$ involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, record the remainder.\n2. Divide the quotient from the previous step by 5, record the remainder.\n3. Repeat step 2 until the quotient is 0.\n4. The base-5 representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform this conversion using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base-5 representation of the decimal number $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert a decimal number (base 10) to another base (in this case, base 5), we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide the number by the new base.\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient of the division.\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 until the quotient is 0.\n5. The base-5 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform these steps for the number 555 in base 10 to convert it to base 5.\n\nWe will use Python to ensure the accuracy of the conversion.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    \n    # The remainders give the digits of the number in the new base in reverse order.\n    digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(map(str, digits))\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_number = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) converted to base 5 is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) to base \\(5\\), we need to repeatedly divide the number by \\(5\\) and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base \\(5\\) representation. Let\'s do this step by step.\n\n1. Divide \\(555\\) by \\(5\\):\n\\[555 \\div 5 = 111 \\text{ remainder } 0\\]\n\n2. Divide \\(111\\) by \\(5\\):\n\\[111 \\div 5 = 22 \\text{ remainder } 1\\]\n\n3. Divide \\(22\\) by \\(5\\):\n\\[22 \\div 5 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\n\n4. Divide \\(4\\) by \\(5\\):\n\\[4 \\div 5 = 0 \\text{ remainder } 4\\]\n\nThe remainders, read in reverse order, give us the base \\(5\\) representation: \\(4210_5\\).\n\nSo, \\(555_{10} = 4210_5\\).\n\nLet\'s verify this by writing the Python code to perform the conversion.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_5(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    base_5_digits = []\n    \n    while n > 0:\n        remainder = n % 5\n        base_5_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        n = n // 5\n    \n    # The remainders give the base 5 number in reverse order\n    base_5_digits.reverse()\n    return \'\'.join(base_5_digits)\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base_5(555)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base \\(5\\) representation of \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'Let\'s start by understanding the problem. We need to convert the decimal number 555 to its base 5 representation.\n\nThe steps to convert a decimal number to a different base are as follows:\n1. Divide the number by the new base (in this case, 5).\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient from the division.\n4. Repeat the process until the quotient is 0.\n5. The base 5 representation is the sequence of remainders read in reverse order.\n\nLet\'s implement this in Python using a loop to perform the conversion.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    \n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    \n    # The base 5 representation is the reverse of the collected remainders\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base 5 representation of the decimal number 555 is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process for $555_{10}$ to base $5$ involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide the number by 5 and record the remainder.\n2. Update the number to the quotient of the division.\n3. Repeat steps 1 and 2 until the quotient is 0.\n4. The base-5 representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s implement this process in Python to get the accurate result.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base-5 representation of $555_{10}$ is $\\boxed{4210_5}$.', 'To convert the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) to base \\(5\\), we need to repeatedly divide the number by \\(5\\) and keep track of the remainders. The remainders, read in reverse order, will give us the base \\(5\\) representation.\n\nHere are the steps:\n\n1. Divide \\(555\\) by \\(5\\), which gives \\(111\\) with a remainder of \\(0\\).\n2. Divide \\(111\\) by \\(5\\), which gives \\(22\\) with a remainder of \\(1\\).\n3. Divide \\(22\\) by \\(5\\), which gives \\(4\\) with a remainder of \\(2\\).\n4. Divide \\(4\\) by \\(5\\), which gives \\(0\\) with a remainder of \\(4\\).\n\nReading the remainders in reverse order, we get \\(4210_5\\).\n\nLet\'s confirm this by implementing the conversion in Python.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base):\n    if decimal_number == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while decimal_number:\n        digits.append(int(decimal_number % base))\n        decimal_number //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base_n(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base \\(5\\) representation of the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) to base \\(5\\), we repeatedly divide the number by \\(5\\) and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process involves the following steps:\n\n1. Divide the number by \\(5\\).\n2. Record the remainder.\n3. Update the number to the quotient from the division.\n4. Repeat steps 1-3 until the quotient is \\(0\\).\n5. The base \\(5\\) representation is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform this conversion using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_representation = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_representation)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe base \\(5\\) representation of the decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number (base 10) to a different base, we can use repeated division by the new base. The remainders from each division step give us the digits of the number in the new base, starting from the least significant digit (rightmost) to the most significant digit (leftmost).\n\nHere\'s how we can convert \\(555_{10}\\) to base 5:\n\n1. Divide 555 by 5, record the remainder.\n2. Divide the quotient from step 1 by 5, record the remainder.\n3. Repeat step 2 until the quotient is 0.\n4. The base 5 number is the sequence of remainders read from bottom to top.\n\nLet\'s perform these steps using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\ndef decimal_to_base(n, base):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % base))\n        n //= base\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Convert 555 from base 10 to base 5\ndecimal_number = 555\nbase = 5\nbase_5_number = decimal_to_base(decimal_number, base)\nprint(base_5_number)\n```\n```output\n4210\n```\nThe decimal number \\(555_{10}\\) expressed in base 5 is \\(\\boxed{4210_5}\\).', 'To convert a decimal number to a different base, we repeatedly divide the number by the new base and keep track of the remainders. The conversion process for $555_{10}$ to 