ional(angle_BAC).limit_denominator()\nprint(angle_BAC_fraction)\n```\n```output\n135/7\n```\nThe degree measure of angle \\( \\angle BAC \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{135}{7}}\\).", "To find the volume of the cone, we can use the formula $V = \\frac{1}{3}Bh$, where $B$ is the area of the base and $h$ is the height. Given that the area of the base $B$ is 30 square units and the height $h$ is 6.5 units, we can substitute these values into the formula to find the volume.\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python code.\n\n1. Define the values for the area of the base $B$ and the height $h$.\n2. Substitute these values into the formula for the volume of the cone.\n3. Calculate the volume.\n\nHere's the Python code to perform these steps:\n```python\n# Given values\nB = 30  # area of the base in square units\nh = 6.5  # height in units\n\n# Volume of the cone formula\nV = (1/3) * B * h\n\n# Output the volume\nprint(V)\n```\n```output\n65.0\n```\nThe volume of the cone is \\(\\boxed{65}\\) cubic units.", "The volume \\( V \\) of a cone is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3}Bh \\]\n\nwhere \\( B \\) is the area of the base and \\( h \\) is the height. Given that the area of the base \\( B = 30 \\) square units and the height \\( h = 6.5 \\) units, we can substitute these values into the formula to find the volume.\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\nB = 30  # area of the base in square units\nh = 6.5  # height in units\n\n# Volume of the cone\nV = (1/3) * B * h\nprint(V)\n```\n```output\n65.0\n```\nThe volume of the cone is \\( \\boxed{65} \\) cubic units.", "To find the volume of the cone, we can use the formula \\( V = \\frac{1}{3}Bh \\), where \\( B \\) is the area of the base and \\( h \\) is the height. Given that the area of the base \\( B \\) is 30 square units and the height \\( h \\) is 6.5 units, we can substitute these values into the formula.\n\nLet's calculate it step-by-step using Python.\n```python\n# Gi