te P(-2)\nremainder = P(-2)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe remainder when \\((5x + 9)^{611} + (x + 5)^{11} + (x - 1)^{11} + 3x^2 + 1\\) is divided by \\(x + 2\\) is \\(\\boxed{12}\\).", "Given the conditions \\( |a| = |b| = |c| = |d| = 1 \\) and \\( a + b + c + d = 0 \\), we need to find the maximum value of \\( |(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| \\).\n\nFirst, let's consider the geometric interpretation. Since \\( |a| = |b| = |c| = |d| = 1 \\), the complex numbers \\( a, b, c, \\) and \\( d \\) lie on the unit circle in the complex plane. The condition \\( a + b + c + d = 0 \\) implies that the sum of these four points is zero, which means they form a parallelogram with the origin as the center.\n\nTo maximize \\( |(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| \\), we can use symmetry and the properties of the unit circle. One possible configuration that satisfies the conditions is \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -1 \\), \\( c = i \\), and \\( d = -i \\). This configuration forms a rectangle centered at the origin.\n\nLet's calculate the value of \\( |(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| \\) for this configuration:\n\n\\[\na + b = 1 - 1 = 0, \\quad a + c = 1 + i, \\quad a + d = 1 - i, \\quad b + c = -1 + i, \\quad b + d = -1 - i, \\quad c + d = i - i = 0\n\\]\n\nSince \\( a + b = 0 \\) and \\( c + d = 0 \\), the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n|(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| = |0 \\cdot (1 + i) \\cdot (1 - i) \\cdot (-1 + i) \\cdot (-1 - i) \\cdot 0| = 0\n\\]\n\nThis configuration does not give us the maximum value. Instead, let's consider another configuration, such as \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = -1 \\), \\( c = e^{i\\pi/3} \\), and \\( d = e^{-i\\pi/3} \\). This configuration forms a rhombus centered at the origin.\n\nLet's calculate the value of \\( |(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| \\) for this configuration:\n\n\\[\na + b = 1 - 1 = 0, \\quad a + c = 1 + e^{i\\pi/3}, \\quad a + d = 1 + e^{-i\\pi/3}, \\quad b + c = -1 