ady derived the equation of the line as \\( y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13 \\). So, the slope \\( m \\) is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) and the y-intercept \\( b \\) is \\(-13\\).\n\nTherefore, the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)\\).\n\nLet's box the final answer:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)}\n\\]", "The parameterized line is given by:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx = 8 + 2t \\\\\ny = -1 + 3t\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nTo express the line in the form \\(y = mx + b\\), we need to eliminate the parameter \\(t\\). From the first equation, we can solve for \\(t\\):\n\\[\nt = \\frac{x - 8}{2}\n\\]\nNow substitute this expression for \\(t\\) into the second equation:\n\\[\ny = -1 + 3\\left(\\frac{x - 8}{2}\\right)\n\\]\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\\[\ny = -1 + \\frac{3x - 24}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\ny = -1 + \\frac{3x}{2} - 12\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3x}{2} - 13\n\\]\nSo, the equation of the line in the form \\(y = mx + b\\) is:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13\n\\]\nThus, the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)\\).\n\nLet's confirm this by running the Python code.\n```python\n# Define the parameterized line equations\ndef parameterized_line(t):\n    x = 8 + 2 * t\n    y = -1 + 3 * t\n    return x, y\n\n# Generate some points on the line\npoints = [parameterized_line(t) for t in range(-10, 11)]\n\n# Extract x and y values from the points\nx_values = [point[0] for point in points]\ny_values = [point[1] for point in points]\n\n# Calculate the slope (m) and y-intercept (b)\nfrom scipy.stats import linregress\n\nslope, intercept, r_value, p_value, std_err = linregress(x_values, y_values)\n\nprint(((slope, intercept)))\n```\n```output\n(1.5, -13.0)\n```\nThe Python code confirms that the slope \\(m\\) is \\(\\frac{3}{2}\\) and the y-intercept \\(b\\) is \\(-13\\). Therefore, the ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}, -13\\right)}\n\\]", "To find the equation of the line in the form \\( y = mx + b \\) from the given parameterized line, we need to eliminate the parameter \\( t \\) and express \\( y \\) in terms of \\( x \\).\n\nThe parameterized line is given by:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx = 8 + 2t \\\\\ny = -1 + 3t\n\\end{cases}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we solve the \\( x \\)-equation for \\( t \\):\n\\[\nt = \\frac{x - 8}{2}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute this expression for \\( t \\) into the \\( y \\)-equation:\n\\[\ny = -1 + 3 \\left( \\frac{x - 8}{2} \\right).\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side, we get:\n\\[\ny = -1 + \\frac{3x - 24}{2} = -1 + \\frac{3x}{2} - 12 = \\frac{3x}{2} - 13.\n\\]\n\nThus, the equation of the line is \\( y = \\frac{3}{2}x - 13 \\). The ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left( \\frac{3}{2}, -13 \\right)\\).\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing the steps in Python.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the symbols\nx, y, t = symbols('x y t')\n\n# Define the parameterized equations\nx_eq = Eq(x, 8 + 2*t)\ny_eq = Eq(y, -1 + 3*t)\n\n# Solve the x equation for t\nt_expr = solve(x_eq, t)[0]\n\n# Substitute t into the y equation\ny_expr = y_eq.subs(t, t_expr)\n\n# Simplify the expression to get y in terms of x\ny_simplified = y_expr.rhs.simplify()\n\n# Extract the slope (m) and y-intercept (b)\nm = y_simplified.as_coefficients_dict()[x]\nb = y_simplified.as_coefficients_dict()[1]\n\nprint(((m, b)))\n```\n```output\n(3/2, -13)\n```\nThe ordered pair \\((m, b)\\) is \\(\\left( \\frac{3}{2}, -13 \\right)\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left( \\frac{3}{2}, -13 \\right)}\n\\]", "The given parameterization of the line is:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -1 \