 surface area \\( A \\) of a cube is given by the formula \\( A = 6s^2 \\). Since \\( s = 1 \\) foot, the surface area is:\n\\[ A = 6 \\times 1^2 = 6 \\text{ square feet} \\]\n\nSince we need the surface area in square inches, we need to convert square feet to square inches. There are 144 square inches in a square foot (since \\( 1 \\text{ foot} = 12 \\text{ inches} \\) and \\( 12^2 = 144 \\)). Therefore, the surface area in square inches is:\n\\[ A = 6 \\times 144 = 864 \\text{ square inches} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given volume of the cube in cubic feet\nvolume_cubic_feet = 1\n\n# Calculate the side length of the cube in feet\nside_length_feet = volume_cubic_feet ** (1/3)\n\n# Calculate the surface area of the cube in square feet\nsurface_area_square_feet = 6 * (side_length_feet ** 2)\n\n# Convert the surface area to square inches (1 square foot = 144 square inches)\nsurface_area_square_inches = surface_area_square_feet * 144\n\nprint(surface_area_square_inches)\n```\n```output\n864.0\n```\nThe total surface area of the cube with a volume of 1 cubic foot is \\(\\boxed{864}\\) square inches.", "To find the total surface area of a cube with a volume of 1 cubic foot, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the side length of the cube.\n2. Calculate the surface area of the cube.\n\nFirst, we know that the volume \\(V\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by:\n\\[ V = s^3 \\]\n\nGiven that the volume \\(V\\) is 1 cubic foot, we can solve for \\(s\\):\n\\[ s = \\sqrt[3]{1} = 1 \\text{ foot} \\]\n\nNext, the surface area \\(A\\) of a cube with side length \\(s\\) is given by:\n\\[ A = 6s^2 \\]\n\nSubstituting \\(s = 1\\) foot into the formula, we get:\n\\[ A = 6 \\times (1 \\text{ foot})^2 = 6 \\text{ square feet} \\]\n\nSince we need the surface area in square inches, we need to convert square feet to square inches. There are 12 inches in a foot, so there are \\(12^2 = 144\\) square inches in a square foot. Therefore:\n\