ulate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers\nn = 2003\na_n = 2 * n - 1\nprint(a_n)\n```\n```output\n4005\n```\nThe 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers is \\(\\boxed{4005}\\).", "To find the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers, we can use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence. The general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ a_n = a_1 + (n-1) \\cdot d \\]\nwhere:\n- \\(a_n\\) is the \\(n\\)-th term,\n- \\(a_1\\) is the first term,\n- \\(d\\) is the common difference, and\n- \\(n\\) is the term number.\n\nFor the sequence of odd numbers, the first term \\(a_1\\) is 1, and the common difference \\(d\\) is 2. We need to find the 2003rd term, so \\(n = 2003\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ a_{2003} = 1 + (2003-1) \\cdot 2 \\]\n\\[ a_{2003} = 1 + 2002 \\cdot 2 \\]\n\\[ a_{2003} = 1 + 4004 \\]\n\\[ a_{2003} = 4005 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the first term and the common difference\na1 = 1\nd = 2\nn = 2003\n\n# Calculate the 2003rd term\na_n = a1 + (n - 1) * d\nprint(a_n)\n```\n```output\n4005\n```\nThe 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers is \\(\\boxed{4005}\\).", "To find the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers, we can use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence. The sequence of odd numbers is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a_1\\) is 1 and the common difference \\(d\\) is 2. The general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\n\\[a_n = a_1 + (n-1) \\cdot d\\]\n\nFor this specific sequence, the first term \\(a_1 = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 2\\). We need to find the 2003rd term, so \\(n = 2003\\). Plugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[a_{2003} = 1 + (2003-1) \\cdot 2\\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the fir