 } n \\geq 5.\\]\n\nWe are given the initial values:\n\\[x_1 = 211, \\quad x_2 = 375, \\quad x_3 = 420, \\quad x_4 = 523.\\]\n\nTo find the value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\), we need to determine the sequence values up to these indices. However, since the recurrence relation involves four previous terms, the sequence will exhibit periodic behavior after a certain number of terms. Let's calculate the first few terms of the sequence to identify any periodicity:\n\n\\[x_5 = x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267,\\]\n\\[x_6 = x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211,\\]\n\\[x_7 = x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375,\\]\n\\[x_8 = x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420,\\]\n\\[x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523,\\]\n\\[x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267,\\]\n\\[x_{11} = x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211,\\]\n\\[x_{12} = x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\\]\n\nWe can see that \\(x_{11} = x_1\\) and \\(x_{12} = x_2\\), which suggests that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. Therefore, we can find \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) by determining their positions within the period:\n\n\\[531 \\mod 10 = 1,\\]\n\\[753 \\mod 10 = 3,\\]\n\\[975 \\mod 10 = 5.\\]\n\nSo, \\(x_{531} = x_1 = 211\\), \\(x_{753} = x_3 = 420\\), and \\(x_{975} = x_5 = 267\\).\n\nFinally, we can find the sum:\n\n\\[x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 211 + 420 + 267 = 898.\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Calculate the first 10 terms to confirm the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 14):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# The sequence is periodic with period 10\nperiod = 10\n\n# Find the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[531 % period]\nx_753 = x[753 