\\\nx_3 &= 420, \\\\\nx_4 &= 523, \\\\\nx_5 &= x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\\\\nx_6 &= x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\\\\nx_7 &= x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\\\\nx_8 &= x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\\\\nx_9 &= x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\\\\nx_{10} &= x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\\\\nx_{11} &= x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\\\\nx_{12} &= x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe observe that \\(x_{11} = x_1\\) and \\(x_{12} = x_2\\). This suggests that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. To confirm this, we can check the next few terms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_{13} &= x_{12} - x_{11} + x_{10} - x_9 = 375 - 211 + (-267) - (-523) = 420, \\\\\nx_{14} &= x_{13} - x_{12} + x_{11} - x_{10} = 420 - 375 + 211 - (-267) = 523, \\\\\nx_{15} &= x_{14} - x_{13} + x_{12} - x_{11} = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\\\\nx_{16} &= x_{15} - x_{14} + x_{13} - x_{12} = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\\\\nx_{17} &= x_{16} - x_{15} + x_{14} - x_{13} = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\\\\nx_{18} &= x_{17} - x_{16} + x_{15} - x_{14} = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\\\\nx_{19} &= x_{18} - x_{17} + x_{16} - x_{15} = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\\\\nx_{20} &= x_{19} - x_{18} + x_{17} - x_{16} = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\\\\nx_{21} &= x_{20} - x_{19} + x_{18} - x_{17} = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\\\\nx_{22} &= x_{21} - x_{20} + x_{19} - x_{18} = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe see that the sequence indeed repeats every 10 terms. Therefore, we can find \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) by determining their positions within the repeating cycle:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n531 \\mod 10 &= 1, \\\\\n753 \\mod 10 &= 3, \\\\\n975 \\mod 10 &= 5.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus, \\(x_{531} = x_1 = 211\\), \\(x_{753} = x_3 = 420\\), and \\(x_{975} = x_5 = 267\\). Therefore, the value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is:\n\n\\[\nx_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 211 + 420 + 267 = 898.\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the initial terms of the sequence\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Compute the next terms until we have at least 10 terms\nfor n in range(4, 10):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# The sequence is periodic with period 10\nperiod = 10\n\n# Find the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[(531 - 1) % period]\nx_753 = x[(753 - 1) % period]\nx_975 = x[(975 - 1) % period]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to compute the sequence values based on the given recurrence relation. The recurrence relation is defined as follows:\n\\[ x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4} \\text{ for } n \\geq 5. \\]\nWe are given the initial values:\n\\[ x_1 = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_2 = 375, \\]\n\\[ x_3 = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_4 = 523. \\]\nWe need to find the values of \\( x_{531} \\), \\( x_{753} \\), and \\( x_{975} \\) and then compute their sum.\n\nFirst, let's generate the sequence values up to a few terms to see if there is any periodicity or pattern. If we find a pattern, we can use it to directly find the values of \\( x_{531} \\), \\( x_{753} \\), and \\( x_{975} \\).\n\nLet's write a Python code to generate the sequence and find the values of \\( x_{531} \\), \\( x_{753} \\), and \\( x_{975} \\).\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Generate the sequence up to x_1000 to check for periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 1000):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# Find the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 =