 terms of the sequence to identify any patterns:\n\n\\[ x_5 = x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267 \\]\n\\[ x_6 = x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211 \\]\n\\[ x_7 = x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375 \\]\n\\[ x_8 = x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420 \\]\n\\[ x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523 \\]\n\\[ x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267 \\]\n\\[ x_{11} = x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211 \\]\n\\[ x_{12} = x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375 \\]\n\\[ x_{13} = x_{12} - x_{11} + x_{10} - x_9 = 375 - 211 + (-267) - (-523) = 420 \\]\n\\[ x_{14} = x_{13} - x_{12} + x_{11} - x_{10} = 420 - 375 + 211 - (-267) = 523 \\]\n\nWe can see that \\( x_{11} = x_1 \\), \\( x_{12} = x_2 \\), \\( x_{13} = x_3 \\), and \\( x_{14} = x_4 \\). This indicates that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. Therefore, we can find \\( x_{531} \\), \\( x_{753} \\), and \\( x_{975} \\) by determining their positions within the period:\n\n\\[ x_{531} = x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211 \\]\n\\[ x_{753} = x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420 \\]\n\\[ x_{975} = x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} \\) is:\n\n\\[ 211 + 420 + 267 = 898 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this by writing the Python code to compute the sequence and verify the periodicity.\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Compute the next terms until we see the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 20):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# Check the periodicity\nprint(x)\n```\n```output\n[211, 375, 420, 523, 267, -211, -375, -420, -523, -267, 211, 375, 420, 523, 267, -211, -375, -420, -523, -267]\n```\nThe computed sequence confirms the periodicity with a period of 10. The sequence repeats every 10 terms as follows: \\([211, 375, 420, 523, 267, -211, 