f the possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(|x-4| - 10 = 2\\), we first isolate the absolute value term:\n\n\\[|x-4| = 12\\]\n\nThis absolute value equation can be split into two separate linear equations:\n\n\\[x-4 = 12 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x-4 = -12\\]\n\nWe solve each equation separately:\n\n1. \\(x-4 = 12\\)\n\\[x = 12 + 4\\]\n\\[x = 16\\]\n\n2. \\(x-4 = -12\\)\n\\[x = -12 + 4\\]\n\\[x = -8\\]\n\nSo, the two possible values of \\(x\\) are \\(16\\) and \\(-8\\). The product of these values is:\n\n\\[16 \\times (-8) = -128\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Solving the equation |x-4| - 10 = 2\r\n# First, isolate the absolute value term\r\n# |x-4| = 12\r\n# This gives us two equations: x-4 = 12 and x-4 = -12\r\n\r\n# Solving x-4 = 12\r\nx1 = 12 + 4\r\n\r\n# Solving x-4 = -12\r\nx2 = -12 + 4\r\n\r\n# Calculating the product of the solutions\r\nproduct_of_solutions = x1 * x2\r\nprint(product_of_solutions)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(|x-4| - 10 = 2\\), we first isolate the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[|x-4| = 12\\]\n\nThe equation \\(|x-4| = 12\\) means that \\(x-4 = 12\\) or \\(x-4 = -12\\). We can solve these two equations separately:\n\n1. \\(x-4 = 12\\)\n2. \\(x-4 = -12\\)\n\nLet's solve these equations using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Solve the equations x-4 = 12 and x-4 = -12\nx1 = 12 + 4\nx2 = -12 + 4\n\n# Calculate the product of the solutions\nproduct_of_solutions = x1 * x2\nprint((x1, x2, product_of_solutions))\n```\n```output\n(16, -8, -128)\n```\nThe solutions to the equation \\(|x-4| - 10 = 2\\) are \\(x = 16\\) and \\(x = -8\\). The product of these solutions is:\n\n\\[16 \\times (-8) = -128\\]\n\nSo, the product of all possible values of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "