ea of the larger circle minus the area of the smaller circle and the area of the segment of the larger circle that is not shaded. The area of the segment of the larger circle that is not shaded is the area of the sector minus the area of the triangle formed by the two radii and the chord connecting the endpoints of the arc.\n\n   The area of the sector of the larger circle with central angle $\\theta$ is $\\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\cdot 4\\pi$. The area of the triangle is $\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta) = 2\\sin(\\theta)$. So the area of the segment is $\\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\cdot 4\\pi - 2\\sin(\\theta)$.\n\n   The area of the shaded region is then:\n   \\[\n   4\\pi - \\pi - \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{360^\\circ} \\cdot 4\\pi - 2\\sin(\\theta)\\right) = 3\\pi - \\left(\\frac{\\theta}{90^\\circ} \\cdot \\pi - 2\\sin(\\theta)\\right).\n   \\]\n   Setting this equal to $\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$, we get:\n   \\[\n   3\\pi - \\frac{\\theta}{90^\\circ} \\cdot \\pi + 2\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}.\n   \\]\n   Simplifying, we get:\n   \\[\n   3\\pi - \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{90} + 2\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}.\n   \\]\n   Rearranging terms, we get:\n   \\[\n   3\\pi - \\frac{5\\pi}{3} = \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{90} - 2\\sin(\\theta).\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the left side, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9\\pi - 5\\pi}{3} = \\frac{4\\pi}{3}.\n   \\]\n   So we have:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4\\pi}{3} = \\frac{\\theta \\pi}{90} - 2\\sin(\\theta).\n   \\]\n   Dividing through by $\\pi$, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{4}{3} = \\frac{\\theta}{90} - 2\\sin(\\theta).\n   \\]\n   This equation can be solved numerically. Let's use Python to find the value of $\\theta$.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import fsolve\n\n# Define the equation to solve\ndef equation(theta):\n    return (theta / 90) - 2 * np.sin(theta) - 4 / 3\n\n# Initial guess for theta\ninitial_guess = 100\n\n# Solve the equation\ntheta_solution = fsolve(equation, initial_guess)[0]\nprint(