erator / sqrt(5)\r\n\r\n# Take the square root of the simplified fraction\r\nfinal_result = simplify(sqrt(fraction_inside_sqrt))\r\n\r\nprint(final_result)\n```\n```output\n13/6\n```\nThe simplified fraction is indeed \\(\\frac{13}{6}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{13}{6}}\n\\]", "To solve the given expression, we will break it down step-by-step and use Python to ensure accuracy. The expression we need to simplify is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} + \\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} + \\sqrt{45}}{\\sqrt{5}}}\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify the individual components inside the square root:\n\n1. Simplify \\(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{80}} = \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16 \\cdot 5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5}{4\\sqrt{5}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{20} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}\n\\]\n\n2. Simplify \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{845} = \\sqrt{169 \\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{169} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 13\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{845}}{9} = \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9}\n\\]\n\n3. Simplify \\(\\sqrt{45}\\):\n\\[\n\\sqrt{45} = \\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{9} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nNow we can substitute these simplified forms back into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]\n\nCombine the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4} + \\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{9} + 3\\sqrt{5} = \\sqrt{5} \\left( \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{13}{9} + 3 \\right)\n\\]\n\nFind a common denominator for the fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{9}{36}, \\quad \\frac{13}{9} = \\frac{52}{36}, \\quad 3 = \\frac{108}{36}\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{13}{9} + 3 = \\frac{9}{36} + \\frac{52}{36} + \\frac{108}{36} = \\frac{169}{36}\n\\]\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{5} \\left( \\frac{169}{36} \\right)\n\\]\nNow, divide by \\(\\sqrt{5}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5} \\left( \\frac{169}{36} \\right)}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{169}{36}\n