.\n\nThus, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "Given the expression:\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{2} = a + \\cfrac{1}{b + \\cfrac{1}{c + \\cfrac{1}{d + \\dotsb}}}\n\\]\nwhere \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), \\(d\\) are positive integers, we need to compute \\(b\\).\n\nTo solve this, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Compute the value of \\(\\sqrt[3]{2}\\).\n2. Find the integer part of \\(\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) to determine \\(a\\).\n3. Subtract \\(a\\) from \\(\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) and take the reciprocal to find the next term in the continued fraction.\n4. Repeat the process to find \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and so on.\n\nLet's implement this in Python using the sympy library to handle the symbolic and numerical computations.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Compute the value of the cube root of 2\ncube_root_2 = sp.Rational(2)**(sp.Rational(1, 3))\n\n# Find the integer part of the cube root of 2 to determine a\na = sp.floor(cube_root_2)\n\n# Compute the fractional part and take the reciprocal to find the next term in the continued fraction\nfractional_part = cube_root_2 - a\nreciprocal = 1 / fractional_part\n\n# Find the integer part of the reciprocal to determine b\nb = sp.floor(reciprocal)\n\n# Print the value of b\nprint(b)\n```\n```output\n1\n```\nThe value of \\( b \\) in the continued fraction representation of \\(\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to express $\\sqrt[3]{2}$ as a continued fraction of the form $a + \\cfrac{1}{b + \\cfrac{1}{c + \\cfrac{1}{d + \\dotsb}}}$. We can find the integer part of $\\sqrt[3]{2}$ first, and then work on the fractional part to find the subsequent terms of the continued fraction.\n\n1. First, we find the integer part of $\\sqrt[3]{2}$. Since $1^3 = 1$ and $2^3 = 8$, we know that $1 < \\sqrt[3]{2} < 2$. Therefore, the integer part $a$ is 1.\n2. Next, we subtract the integer part from $\\sqrt[3]{2}$ and take the reciprocal to find the next term in the continued fraction:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{2} - 1}\n   \