|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)$.\n4. Dividing both sides by $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|$, we get $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)$.\n5. Now, we need to find the angle $\\theta$ between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$. Using the dot product formula again, we have $\\", "To solve this problem, we need to use the properties of vectors and the dot product. Let's denote the vectors as $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$, and let $\\theta$ be the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$. We are given that the angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $29^\\circ$ and the angle between $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is $84^\\circ$.\n\nThe dot product of two vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = \\|\\mathbf{u}\\| \\|\\mathbf{v}\\| \\cos \\phi$, where $\\phi$ is the angle between the vectors.\n\nUsing this, we can write the following equations based on the given angles:\n1. $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ$\n2. $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 84^\\circ$\n3. $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos \\theta$\n\nFrom equation 2, we can expand the dot product:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 84^\\circ\n\\]\nUsing the first equation, we can substitute $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a}$ with $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ$:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 84^\\circ\n\\]\nDividing both sides by $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|$:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 84^\\circ\n\\]\nNow, we need to find the angle $\\theta$ between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$. From the third equation:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nExpanding the dot product:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nUsing the first equation, we can substitute $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$ with $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ$:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|^2 - \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nDividing both sides by $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\|$:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ = \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nWe already have an expression for $\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 84^\\circ$ from earlier:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 84^\\circ = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|\n\\]\nSo we can substitute this into the equation for $\\cos \\theta$:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ = \\frac{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}{\\cos 84^\\circ} \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nSolving for $\\cos \\theta$:\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{(\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ) \\cos 84^\\circ}{\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos 29^\\circ - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|}\n\\]\nSince we don't know the magnitudes of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$, we can simplify by assuming $\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| = 1$ and $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = 1$ (this is valid because the angles are independent of the magnitudes):\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{(1 - \\cos 29^\\circ) \\cos 84^\\circ}{\\cos 29^\\circ - 1}\n\\]\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given angles in degrees\nangle_ab = 29\nangle_b_ab_minus_b = 84\n\n# Convert angles to radians\n