ed to use vector properties and the dot product. Let's denote the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ as $\\theta_{ab} = 29^\\circ$ and the angle between $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ as $\\theta_{b(a-b)} = 84^\\circ$. We need to find the angle $\\theta_{a(a-b)}$ between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$.\n\nFirst, we can use the dot product to express the given angles:\n1. The dot product of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{b}| \\cos(29^\\circ)$.\n2. The dot product of $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = |\\mathbf{b}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(84^\\circ)$. This can be expanded to $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{b}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(84^\\circ)$, or $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} - |\\mathbf{b}|^2 = |\\mathbf{b}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(84^\\circ)$.\n3. The dot product of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(\\theta_{a(a-b)})$. This can be expanded to $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(\\theta_{a(a-b)})$, or $|\\mathbf{a}|^2 - \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = |\\mathbf{a}| |\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}| \\cos(\\theta_{a(a-b)})$.\n\nLet's solve this step by step using Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\nimport math\n\n# Define the symbols\na_dot_b, a_magnitude, b_magnitude, a_minus_b_magnitude, theta_ab, theta_ba_minus_b, theta_a_a_minus_b = sp.symbols('a_dot_b a_magnitude b_magnitude a_minus_b_magnitude theta_ab theta_ba_minus_b theta_a_a_minus_b')\n\n# Given angles in degrees\ntheta_ab_value = 29\ntheta_ba_minus_b_value = 84\n\n# Convert angles to radians\ntheta_ab_rad = math.radians(theta_ab_value)\ntheta_ba_minus_b_rad 