lues\nn = 31\nk = 28\n\n# Calculate the binomial coefficient using math.comb which is available in Python 3.8+\nbinomial_coefficient = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(binomial_coefficient)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe binomial coefficient \\(\\binom{31}{28}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4495}\n\\]", "To compute \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\), we can use the formula for combinations:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 31\\) and \\(k = 28\\). So, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nWe can calculate this step by step. Let's use Python to ensure the accuracy of our result.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the combination using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\ncombination = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(combination)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\) is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", "To compute $\\binom{31}{28}$, we can use the formula for combinations:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, $n = 31$ and $k = 28$. So we have:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28!(31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nLet's calculate this step by step using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the combination using the formula\nn = 31\nk = 28\ncombination = math.comb(n, k)\nprint(combination)\n```\n```output\n4495\n```\nThe value of $\\binom{31}{28}$ is \\(\\boxed{4495}\\).", "To compute \\(\\dbinom{31}{28}\\), we can use the formula for binomial coefficients:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nIn this case, \\(n = 31\\) and \\(k = 28\\), so:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{31}{28} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot (31-28)!} = \\frac{31!}{28! \\cdot 3!} = \\frac{31 \\times 30 \\times 29}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1}\n\\]\n\nWe can calculate this step by step. Let's start by computing the numerator \\(31 \\times 30 \\times