eter of triangle \\( ABC \\).\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\ncos_theta = sp.symbols('cos_theta')\n\n# Equation derived from the Law of Sines and right triangle properties\nequation = sp.Eq(cos_theta, (4*cos_theta**2 - 1) / cos_theta)\n\n# Solve the equation\nsolution = sp.solve(equation, cos_theta)\ncos_theta_value = solution[1]  # We take the positive solution\n\n# Calculate x and y\nx = (4*cos_theta_value**2 - 1) / cos_theta_value\ny = x * cos_theta_value\n\n# Perimeter of triangle ABC\nperimeter = 2*x + 2*y\nprint(perimeter.evalf())\n```\n```output\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the solution list. Let's carefully re-evaluate the equation and ensure we are solving it correctly. The equation we derived is:\n\n\\[ \\cos \\theta = \\frac{4 \\cos^2 \\theta - 1}{\\cos \\theta} \\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[ \\cos^2 \\theta = 4 \\cos^2 \\theta - 1 \\]\n\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\n\\[ 3 \\cos^2 \\theta = 1 \\]\n\nSo:\n\n\\[ \\cos^2 \\theta = \\frac{1}{3} \\]\n\nTaking the positive square root (since \\(\\cos \\theta\\) must be positive in this context), we get:\n\n\\[ \\cos \\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\]\n\nNow we can substitute this back into the expressions for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{4 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right) - 1}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} = \\frac{\\frac{4}{3} - 1}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\cdot 3 = \\sqrt{3} \\]\n\n\\[ y = x \\cos \\theta = \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} = 1 \\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(ABC\\) is \\(2x + 2y = 2\\sqrt{3} + 2 \\cdot 1 = 2\\sqrt{3} + 2\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\ncos_theta = sp.symbols('cos_theta')\n\n# Equation derived from the Law of Sines and right triangle properties\nequation = sp.Eq(cos_theta, (4*cos_theta**2 - 1) / cos_theta)\n\n# Sol