nd{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$ is \\(\\boxed{-41}\\).", "To find the dot product of two vectors $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}$, we use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3\n\\]\n\nGiven vectors are $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$. Substituting the components into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-2) \\cdot 3 + 0 \\cdot 4 + 7 \\cdot (-5)\n\\]\n\nNow we can compute this step by step:\n\n\\[\n(-2) \\cdot 3 = -6\n\\]\n\\[\n0 \\cdot 4 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\cdot (-5) = -35\n\\]\n\nSo the dot product is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = -6 + 0 + (-35) = -6 - 35 = -41\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the vectors\na = [-2, 0, 7]\nb = [3, 4, -5]\n\n# Calculate the dot product\ndot_product = sum(x*y for x, y in zip(a, b))\nprint(dot_product)\n```\n```output\n-41\n```\nThe dot product of the vectors $\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$ is \\(\\boxed{-41}\\).", "To find the dot product of two vectors, we need to multiply the corresponding components of the vectors and then sum the results. The dot product of two vectors $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3\n\\]\n\nFor the vectors $\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}$, the dot product is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = (-2) \\cdot 3 + 0 \\cdot 4 + 7 \\cdot (-5) = -6 + 0 - 35 = -41\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Py