s digit is } 4)\\]\n\\[4^4 = 256 \\quad (\\text{units digit is } 6)\\]\nSo, the units digit of \\(4^n\\) is 4 if \\(n\\) is odd and 6 if \\(n\\) is even. Since \\(24^{24}\\) is clearly even, the units digit of \\(4^{24^{24}}\\) is 6.\n\nTherefore, the units digit of \\(4\\$\\) is \\(6\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code for accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to find the units digit of a^b\r\ndef units_digit(a, b):\r\n    # Get the units digit of the base\r\n    a_units = a % 10\r\n    # If the exponent is 0, the units digit is 1 (except for 0^0 which is undefined)\r\n    if b == 0:\r\n        return 1\r\n    # Find the units digit of the power\r\n    if a_units == 0:\r\n        return 0\r\n    elif a_units == 1:\r\n        return 1\r\n    elif a_units == 2:\r\n        if b % 4 == 0:\r\n            return 6\r\n        elif b % 4 == 1:\r\n            return 2\r\n        elif b % 4 == 2:\r\n            return 4\r\n        else:\r\n            return 8\r\n    elif a_units == 3:\r\n        if b % 4 == 0:\r\n            return 1\r\n        elif b % 4 == 1:\r\n            return 3\r\n        elif b % 4 == 2:\r\n            return 9\r\n        else:\r\n            return 7\r\n    elif a_units == 4:\r\n        if b % 2 == 0:\r\n            return 6\r\n        else:\r\n            return 4\r\n    elif a_units == 5:\r\n        return 5\r\n    elif a_units == 6:\r\n        return 6\r\n    elif a_units == 7:\r\n        if b % 4 == 0:\r\n            return 1\r\n        elif b % 4 == 1:\r\n            return 7\r\n        elif b % 4 == 2:\r\n            return 9\r\n        else:\r\n            return 3\r\n    elif a_units == 8:\r\n        if b % 4 == 0:\r\n            return 6\r\n        elif b % 4 == 1:\r\n            return 8\r\n        elif b % 4 == 2:\r\n            return 4\r\n        else:\r\n            return 2\r\n    elif a_units == 9:\r\n        if b % 2 == 0:\r\n            return 1\r\n        else:\r\n            return 9\r\n\r\n# Calculate 4!\r\nfactorial_4 = 24\r\n# Calculate the units digit of 4^(24^24)\r\nunits_digit_4_power = units_digit(4, factorial_4 ** factorial_4)\r\nprint(units_digit_4_power)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe units digit of \\(4\\$\\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).", "To find the units digit of $4\\$$, we need to understand the definition of the superfactorial. The superfactorial $n\\$ is defined as a power tower of $n!$ that is $n!$ high. Specifically, for $4\\$$, we have:\n\\[4\\$ = 4!^{4!^{4!^{4!}}}.\\]\nFirst, we need to determine the units digit of $4!$. Since $4! = 24$, the units digit of $4!$ is $4$. Therefore, we need to find the units digit of the power tower $24^{24^{24^{24}}}$. Since the units digit of $24$ is $4$, we can simplify this to finding the units digit of $4^{24^{24^{24}}}$.\n\nNext, we need to determine the units digit of $4^{24^{24^{24}}}$. The units digits of powers of $4$ cycle every 2: $4^1 = 4$, $4^2 = 16$, $4^3 = 64$, $4^4 = 256$, and so on. So, we need to determine whether the exponent $24^{24^{24}}$ is even or odd. Since $24$ is even, any power of $24$ will also be even. Therefore, $24^{24^{24}}$ is even.\n\nSince the exponent is even, the units digit of $4^{24^{24^{24}}}$ is the same as the units digit of $4^2$, which is $6$.\n\nThus, the units digit of $4\\$$ is $6$. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Function to find the units digit of 4^n where n is a large power of 24\r\ndef units_digit_of_power(base, exponent):\r\n    # The units digits of powers of 4 cycle every 2: [4, 6]\r\n    units_digits = [4, 6]\r\n    # Find the position in the cycle\r\n    position = (exponent % 2)\r\n    return units_digits[position]\r\n\r\n# Since 24 is even, any power of 24 will also be even\r\n# So, the exponent 24^(24^24) is even\r\nexponent = 24 ** (24 ** 24)\r\n# Find the units digit of 4^(24^(24^24))\r\nunits_digit = units_digit_of_power(4, exponent)\r\nprint(units_digit)\n```\n```output\ntimeout_decorator.timeout_decorator.TimeoutError: 'Timed Out'\n```\nThe units digit of $4\\$$