d the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the modulo operation. The modulo operation gives the remainder of the division of one number by another. In this case, we need to find \\(2004 \\mod 12\\).\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder when 2004 is divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the modulus operator `%` in Python. The expression `2004 % 12` will give us the remainder when 2004 is divided by 12. Let's calculate it.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of 2004 divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the modulo operation. The modulo operation (%) gives the remainder of a division of two numbers. Here's the step-by-step reasoning and the Python code to find the remainder:\n\n1. Perform the division of 2004 by 12.\n2. The remainder of this division is the result we are looking for.\n\nLet's use Python to calculate this.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of 2004 divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the modulus operation. The modulus operation (%) gives the remainder of a division of two numbers. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Perform the division of 2004 by 12.\n2. The remainder of this division is the result we are looking for.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of 2004 divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the modulo operation. The modulo operation (%) gives the remainder of a division of two numbers. So, 2004 % 12 will give the remainder when 2004 is divided by 12.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of 2004 divided by 12 is \\( \\boxed{0} \\).", "To find the remainder of 2004 divided by 12, we can use the modulus operation. The modulus operation (%) gives the remainder of a division of two numbers. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Perform the division of 2004 by 12.\n2. The remainder of this division is the result we are looking for.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004 divided by 12\nremainder = 2004 % 12\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of 2004 divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12, we can use modular arithmetic properties. Specifically, we can simplify the problem by finding the remainder of 2004 divided by 12 and then using that to simplify the exponentiation.\n\n1. First, we find the remainder when 2004 is divided by 12:\n\\[2004 \\div 12 = 167 \\text{ with a remainder of } 0.\\]\nSo, \\(2004 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12}\\).\n\n2. This means that \\(2004^{2004} \\equiv 0^{2004} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12}\\).\n\nTherefore, the remainder when \\(2004^{2004}\\) is divided by 12 is 0.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 2004^2004 divided by 12\nremainder = pow(2004, 2004, 12)\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder of \\(2004^{2004}\\) divided by 12 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", 'To find the remainder when 2004 is divided by 12, we can use the modulus operation. The modulus operation (%) returns the remainder of a division of two numbers. Here is the Python code to find the remainder:\n\n```python\n# Define the number and the divisor\nnumber = 2004\ndivisor = 12\n\n# Calculate t