ulas to find the relationships between the roots of the polynomial.\n\nFor a polynomial $x^4 + 2x^3 + 0x^2 + 0x + 2 = 0$, Vieta's formulas tell us:\n1. The sum of the roots taken one at a time is $-2$.\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time is $0$.\n3. The sum of the product of the roots taken three at a time is $0$.\n4. The product of the roots is $-2$.\n\nGiven these relationships, we can use them to find the expressions $\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4$, $\\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4$, and $\\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3$.\n\nLet's denote the roots as $\\alpha_1, \\alpha_2, \\alpha_3, \\alpha_4$. From Vieta's formulas, we know:\n\\[\n\\alpha_1 + \\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3 + \\alpha_4 = -2\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_1\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = -2\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the values of $\\alpha_1\\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3\\alpha_4$, $\\alpha_1\\alpha_3 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_4$, and $\\alpha_1\\alpha_4 + \\alpha_2\\alpha_3$. Let's denote these expressions as $a$, $b$, and $c$ respectively. Then we have:\n\\[\na + b + c = 0\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = \\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\alpha_4(\\alpha_1 + \\alpha_2 + \\alpha_3 + \\alpha_4) = -2(-2) = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = (\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3)(\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_4)(\\alpha_1\\alpha_3\\alpha_4) = (-2\\alpha_4)(-2\\alpha_3)(-2\\alpha_2) = -8\\alpha_1\\alpha_2\\alpha_3\\alpha_4 = -8(-2) = 16\n\\]\n\nSo we have a system of equations:\n\\[\na + b + c = 0\n\\]\n\\[\nab + bc + ca = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nabc = 16\n\\]\n\nThis is a system of equations for the roots of the polynomial $t^3 - 4t + 16 = 0$. Let's solve this system using Python and `sympy`:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variables\na, b, c = sp.symbols('a