gest_solution >= 2010:\n    largest_solution -= modulus\n\nprint(largest_solution)\n```\n```output\n1992\n```\nThe largest integer less than 2010 that satisfies the given system of congruences is \\(\\boxed{1992}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the largest integer \\( x \\) less than 2010 that satisfies the following system of congruences:\n\\[ x \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ x \\equiv 10 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ x \\equiv 10 \\pmod{13} \\]\n\nFirst, we can combine the last two congruences since they both have the same remainder:\n\\[ x \\equiv 10 \\pmod{11 \\cdot 13} \\]\n\\[ x \\equiv 10 \\pmod{143} \\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\\[ x = 143k + 10 \\]\nfor some integer \\( k \\). Now we need to find \\( k \\) such that:\n\\[ 143k + 10 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ 143k \\equiv -5 \\pmod{7} \\]\nSince \\( 143 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{7} \\), we can simplify this to:\n\\[ 6k \\equiv -5 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ 6k \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} \\]\nTo solve for \\( k \\), we need the modular inverse of 6 modulo 7. The modular inverse of 6 is 6 itself (since \\( 6 \\cdot 6 = 36 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7} \\)). So we get:\n\\[ k \\equiv 6 \\cdot 2 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ k \\equiv 12 \\pmod{7} \\]\n\\[ k \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} \\]\nSo, \\( k = 7m + 5 \\) for some integer \\( m \\). Substituting this back into the equation for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = 143(7m + 5) + 10 \\]\n\\[ x = 1001m + 725 \\]\nTo find the largest \\( x \\) less than 2010, we need:\n\\[ 1001m + 725 < 2010 \\]\n\\[ 1001m < 1285 \\]\n\\[ m < \\frac{1285}{1001} \\approx 1.28 \\]\nSo, the largest possible value for \\( m \\) is 1. Therefore:\n\\[ x = 1001 \\cdot 1 + 725 = 1726 \\]\nLet's verify that 1726 satisfies all the original congruences:\n\\[ 1726 \\div 7 = 246 \\text{ remainder } 5 \\]\n\\[ 1726 \\div 11 = 156 \\text{ remainder } 10 \\]\n\\[ 1726 \\div 13 = 132 \\text{ remainder } 10 \\]\nSince all the conditions are satisfied, the largest integer less than 2010 that meets the criteria is \\(\\boxed{1726}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python c