put\n(8.0, 24.0, 6.0, 8.485281374238571)\n```\nThe calculations confirm that:\n\n- The side length of the equilateral triangle is \\(8\\) cm.\n- The perimeter of the equilateral triangle is \\(24\\) cm.\n- The side length of the square is \\(6\\) cm.\n- The diagonal of the square is approximately \\(8.485\\) cm.\n\nTo express the diagonal in simplest radical form:\n\\[\n\\text{Diagonal} = 6\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of the diagonal of the square is \\(\\boxed{6\\sqrt{2}}\\) cm.", 'Given:\n- The area of the equilateral triangle is \\( 16\\sqrt{3} \\) square centimeters.\n- The perimeters of the square and the equilateral triangle are equal.\n\nWe need to find the length of the diagonal of the square.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Calculate the side length of the equilateral triangle:**\n\n   The area \\( A \\) of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   A = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2\n   \\]\n   Given \\( A = 16\\sqrt{3} \\):\n   \\[\n   16\\sqrt{3} = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( s \\):\n   \\[\n   16\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}} = s^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   64 = s^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   s = \\sqrt{64} = 8 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the perimeter of the equilateral triangle:**\n\n   The perimeter \\( P \\) of the equilateral triangle is:\n   \\[\n   P = 3s = 3 \\times 8 = 24 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the side length of the square:**\n\n   Let the side length of the square be \\( a \\). The perimeter of the square is:\n   \\[\n   4a = 24\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( a \\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{24}{4} = 6 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the length of the diagonal of the square:**\n\n   The diagonal \\( d \\) of a square with side length \\( a \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   d = a\\sqrt{2}\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( a = 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   d = 6\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\nThe length of the diagonal of the square is \\( \\boxed{6\\sqrt{2}} \\) 