es d = 8.\\]\nFrom the first equation, we get:\n\\[5 + b = 8 \\implies b = 3.\\]\nSo, the values are $a = 5$, $b = 3$, $c = 2$, and $d = 8$. We can verify that these values satisfy all the equations:\n1. $5 + 3 = 8$\n2. $2 \\cdot 5 = 5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 5 = 25 \\neq 5 \\cdot 2 = 10$ (This is incorrect, so let\'s try another value for $a$ and $c$).\n\nSince $a$ must be a multiple of 5 and $c$ must be even, the only other possible values are $a = 10/2 = 5$ and $c = 2$. But since $a$ must be from 1 to 9, we need to check if there are other possible values. Let\'s try $a = 10/2 = 5$ and $c = 2$ again, but this time let\'s check the values more carefully.\n\nLet\'s use Python to check all possible values systematically.\n```python\n# We will iterate through all possible values of a, b, c, d from 1 to 9\n# and check which combination satisfies all three equations\n\nfor a in range(1, 10):\n    for c in range(1, 10):\n        if 2 * a == 5 * c:\n            d = 2 * a - c\n            if 1 <= d <= 9 and d != a and d != c:\n                b = d - a\n                if 1 <= b <= 9 and b != a and b != c and b != d:\n                    # We found a valid combination\n                    result = b\n                    print(f"a = {a}, b = {b}, c = {c}, d = {d}")\n                    break\n\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\nNameError: name \'result\' is not defined\n```\nIt seems there was an issue with the code execution. Let\'s try running the code again to find the values of $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ that satisfy the equations.\n```python\n# We will iterate through all possible values of a, b, c, d from 1 to 9\n# and check which combination satisfies all three equations\n\nresult = None\n\nfor a in range(1, 10):\n    for c in range(1, 10):\n        if 2 * a == 5 * c:\n            d = 2 * a - c\n            if 1 <= d <= 9 and d != a and d != c:\n                b = d - a\n                if 1 <= b <= 9 and b != a and b != c and b != d:\n                    # We found a valid combina