e the Python code to verify this solution.\n```python\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = 35\n\n# Possible values for the number of girls (must be a multiple of 13 and less than 35)\npossible_girls = [13, 26]\n\n# Check which value satisfies the conditions\nfor girls in possible_girls:\n    boys = total_students - girls\n    if girls > boys:\n        number_of_boys = boys\n        break\n\nprint(number_of_boys)\n```", "To solve the problem, let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. Let \\( G \\) be the number of girls and \\( B \\) be the number of boys at the meeting.\n2. The total number of students is 35, so we have the equation \\( G + B = 35 \\).\n3. The number of girls \\( G \\) is a multiple of 13, so \\( G \\) can be 13, 26, or 39 (but since the total number of students is 35, \\( G \\) can only be 13 or 26).\n4. We are also given that there are more girls than boys, so \\( G > B \\).\n\nNow, let's check the possible values for \\( G \\):\n\n- If \\( G = 13 \\), then \\( B = 35 - 13 = 22 \\). But \\( G \\) is not greater than \\( B \\) in this case.\n- If \\( G = 26 \\), then \\( B = 35 - 26 = 9 \\). In this case, \\( G > B \\), so this is a valid solution.\n\nTherefore, the number of boys at the meeting is 9. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = 35\n\n# Possible values for the number of girls (multiples of 13)\npossible_girls = [13, 26]\n\n# Check which value satisfies the condition G > B\nfor G in possible_girls:\n    B = total_students - G\n    if G > B:\n        number_of_boys = B\n        break\n\nprint(number_of_boys)\n```\n```output\n9\n```\nThe number of boys at the meeting is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to find the number of boys at the meeting. Let's denote the number of girls as \\( G \\) and the number of boys as \\( B \\). We know the following:\n\n1. The total number of students is 35, so \\( G + B = 35 \\).\n2. The number of girls is a multiple of 13, so \