15.975 = \\frac{15975 \\div 25}{1000 \\div 25} = \\frac{639}{40}\n\\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is $\\frac{639}{40}$ inches.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to find out how many inches on the map correspond to 53.25 miles in real life. Given that 3 inches on the map equate to 10 miles in real life, we can set up a proportion to find the answer.\n\nThe proportion can be set up as follows:\n\\[ \\frac{3 \\text{ inches}}{10 \\text{ miles}} = \\frac{x \\text{ inches}}{53.25 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{3 \\text{ inches} \\times 53.25 \\text{ miles}}{10 \\text{ miles}} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{3 \\times 53.25}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{159.75}{10} \\text{ inches} \\]\n\\[ x = 15.975 \\text{ inches} \\]\n\nExpressing 15.975 as a fraction:\n\\[ 15.975 = \\frac{15975}{1000} = \\frac{639}{40} \\]\n\nSo, the distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\frac{639}{40}\\) inches.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given values\nmap_distance_per_10_miles = 3  # inches\nreal_distance = 53.25  # miles\n\n# Calculate the map distance for 53.25 miles\nmap_distance = (map_distance_per_10_miles * real_distance) / 10\n\n# Convert the map distance to a fraction\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nmap_distance_fraction = Fraction(map_distance).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(map_distance_fraction)\n```\n```output\n639/40\n```\nThe distance between the buildings on the map is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{639}{40}}\\) inches.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the scale of the map and then use it to find the distance between the two buildings on the map.\n\nGiven:\n- 3 inches on the map corresponds to 10 miles in real life.\n- The real-life distance between the two buildings is 53.25 miles.\n\nFirst, we need to find the scale of the map. The scale can be calculated as follows:\n\\[ \\text{Scale} = \\frac{\\text{distance on the map}}{\\text{re