100\\), so their total score is \\(2 \\times 100 = 200\\).\n\nThe total score for the entire class is \\(1600 + 720 + 200 = 2520\\).\n\nThe number of students is \\(30\\).\n\nThe class average is \\(\\frac{2520}{30} = 84\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\n# Total scores\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * 80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * 90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * 100\n\n# Total score of the class\ntotal_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Class average\nclass_average = total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.0\n```\nThe class average on the test is \\(\\boxed{84}\\).", "To find the class average (mean) on the test, we need to calculate the total score of all students and then divide it by the total number of students.\n\nHere's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the 20 students who scored 80.\n2. Calculate the total score of the 8 students who scored 90.\n3. Calculate the total score of the 2 students who scored 100.\n4. Sum these total scores to get the overall total score of the class.\n5. Divide the overall total score by the total number of students (30) to get the class average.\n\nLet's do this calculation using Python.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\n# Total scores\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * 80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * 90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * 100\n\n# Overall total score\noverall_total_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.0\n```\nThe class average (mean) on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.0}\\).", "To find the class average (mean) on the test, we need to calculate the total score of all the students and then divide it by the total number of students. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the 20 students who scored 80.\n2. Calculate the total score of the 8 students who scored 90.\n3. Calculate the total score of the 2 students who scored 100.\n4. Sum these total scores to get the overall total score of the class.\n5. Divide the overall total score by the total number of students (30) to get the class average.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\n# Total scores\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * 80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * 90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * 100\n\n# Overall total score\noverall_total_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Class average\nclass_average = overall_total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```\n```output\n84.0\n```\nThe class average (mean) on the test is \\(\\boxed{84.0}\\).", "To find the class average (mean) on the test, we need to calculate the total score of all students and then divide it by the number of students.\n\nHere's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 80.\n2. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 90.\n3. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 100.\n4. Sum these total scores to get the overall total score.\n5. Divide the overall total score by the total number of students to get the class average.\n\nLet's do this step-by-step using Python code.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\n# Total scores\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * 80\ntotal_sco