te the total score of the students who scored 90:\n\\[ 8 \\text{ students} \\times 90 \\text{ points} = 720 \\text{ points} \\]\n\n3. Calculate the total score of the students who scored 100:\n\\[ 2 \\text{ students} \\times 100 \\text{ points} = 200 \\text{ points} \\]\n\n4. Sum up all the scores to get the total score of the class:\n\\[ 1600 + 720 + 200 = 2520 \\text{ points} \\]\n\n5. Divide the total score by the total number of students to get the average:\n\\[ \\frac{2520 \\text{ points}}{30 \\text{ students}} = 84 \\text{ points} \\]\n\nSo, the class average on this test is \\( \\boxed{84} \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 = 2\n\n# Total scores\ntotal_score_80 = students_80 * 80\ntotal_score_90 = students_90 * 90\ntotal_score_100 = students_100 * 100\n\n# Total score of the class\ntotal_score = total_score_80 + total_score_90 + total_score_100\n\n# Total number of students\ntotal_students = students_80 + students_90 + students_100\n\n# Class average\nclass_average = total_score / total_students\nprint(class_average)\n```", "To find the class average (mean) on the test, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total score of all the students.\n2. Divide the total score by the number of students.\n\nHere's the breakdown of the calculation:\n\n1. \\(20\\) students scored \\(80\\), so their total score is \\(20 \\times 80 = 1600\\).\n2. \\(8\\) students scored \\(90\\), so their total score is \\(8 \\times 90 = 720\\).\n3. \\(2\\) students scored \\(100\\), so their total score is \\(2 \\times 100 = 200\\).\n\nThe total score of all \\(30\\) students is \\(1600 + 720 + 200 = 2520\\).\n\nThe class average is the total score divided by the number of students, which is \\( \\frac{2520}{30} \\).\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of students and their scores\nstudents_80 = 20\nstudents_90 = 8\nstudents_100 