ty, since the faces opposite to each other are symmetric). Then the face opposite to $F$ would be the face with number 6. The probability of obtaining a sum of 7 when two dice are rolled can be calculated by considering all the possible pairs of faces that sum to 7: (1, 6), (2, 5), (3, 4), (4, 3), (5, 2), and (6, 1).\n\nThe probability of obtaining a sum of 7 is given by:\n\n\\[ P(\\text{sum} = 7) = p \\cdot q + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot p = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[ p \\cdot q + \\frac{1}{36} + \\frac{1}{36} + \\frac{1}{36} + \\frac{1}{36} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot p = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ p \\cdot q + \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot p = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\nSince $p + q = \\frac{1}{3}$, we can substitute $q = \\frac{1}{3} - p$ into the equation:\n\n\\[ p \\left( \\frac{1}{3} - p \\right) + \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{1}{6} \\cdot p = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{p}{3} - p^2 + \\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{p}{6} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{2p}{6} + \\frac{p}{6} - p^2 + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{3p}{6} - p^2 + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{p}{2} - p^2 + \\frac{1}{9} = \\frac{47}{288} \\]\n\nMultiplying through by 288 to clear the denominators:\n\n\\[ 144p - 288p^2 + 32 = 47 \\]\n\\[ 288p^2 - 144p + 15 = 0 \\]\n\nWe can solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula $p = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$, where $a = 288$, $b = -144$, and $c = 15$:\n\n\\[ p = \\frac{144 \\pm \\sqrt{(-144)^2 - 4 \\cdot 288 \\cdot 15}}{2 \\cdot 288} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{144 \\pm \\sqrt{20736 - 17280}}{576} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{144 \\pm \\sqrt{3456}}{576} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{144 \\pm 48\\sqrt{3}}{576} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{12 \\pm 4\\sqrt{3}}{48} \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{3}}{12} \\]\n\nSince $p > \\frac{1}{6}$, we take the positive root:\n\n\\[ p = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{12}