nt factored out) is given by \\(-\\frac{a_{n-1}}{a_n}\\). Since \\(a_n = 2\\), this becomes \\(-\\frac{a_{n-1}}{2}\\).\n\nThe product of the roots taken one at a time is given by \\((-1)^n \\frac{a_0}{a_n} = (-1)^n \\frac{66}{2} = (-1)^n \\cdot 33\\). This means the roots must multiply to \\(\\pm 33\\). The possible sets of distinct integer roots that multiply to \\(\\pm 33\\) are \\(\\{1, -1, 3, -3, 11, -11, 33, -33\\}\\).\n\nWe need to find the combination of these roots that minimizes \\(|a_{n-1}|\\). Let's consider the possible combinations of roots and calculate the corresponding \\(a_{n-1}\\) for each combination. The value of \\(a_{n-1}\\) is given by \\(-2 \\sum_{i=1}^n r_i\\).\n\nLet's enumerate the possible combinations and calculate the corresponding \\(|a_{n-1}|\\):\n\n1. Roots: \\(\\{1, -1, 3, -3, 11, -11\\}\\)\n2. Roots: \\(\\{1, -1, 3, -3, 33, -33\\}\\)\n3. Roots: \\(\\{1, -1, 11, -11, 3, -3\\}\\)\n4. Roots: \\(\\{1, -1, 11, -11, 33, -33\\}\\)\n5. Roots: \\(\\{1, 3, -3, 11, -11, 33, -33\\}\\)\n\nWe will calculate \\(|a_{n-1}|\\) for each of these combinations.\n\nLet's write the Python code to do this calculation.\n```python\nimport itertools\n\n# Possible roots that multiply to ±33\npossible_roots = [1, -1, 3, -3, 11, -11, 33, -33]\n\n# Function to calculate |a_{n-1}|\ndef calculate_a_n_minus_1(roots):\n    return abs(2 * sum(roots))\n\n# Find all combinations of roots that multiply to ±33\ncombinations = []\nfor r in range(2, len(possible_roots) + 1):\n    for combo in itertools.combinations(possible_roots, r):\n        if abs(np.prod(combo)) == 33:\n            combinations.append(combo)\n\n# Calculate |a_{n-1}| for each combination and find the minimum\nmin_abs_a_n_minus_1 = float('inf')\nfor combo in combinations:\n    abs_a_n_minus_1 = calculate_a_n_minus_1(combo)\n    if abs_a_n_minus_1 < min_abs_a_n_minus_1:\n        min_abs_a_n_minus_1 = abs_a_n_minus_1\n\nprint(min_abs_a_n_minus_1)\n```\n```output\nNameError: name 'np' is not defined\n```\nI